      "key": "D",
      "text": "Reassurance",
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "explanation": "This is typical uncomplicated infant/early childhood reflux in a thriving child. If there are no red flags such as faltering growth, bilious vomiting, haematemesis, aspiration, or abnormal examination, the best management is reassurance and conservative advice rather than investigations, acid suppression, or specialist referral.",
